  "body": "### Description\n\nrelate #3364 \r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/62551256/234611943-ed596d73-56b9-48c6-bd3a-273934609541.png)\r\nThe image above is the hard disk space usage information of my database.\r\nI don't have a lot of users on my homeserver, there are very few users who join one or two large rooms with thousands of people in other instances.\r\nI was actually wondering if it is possible to clear the status information of a remote room from some time ago and sync it when it is accessed again? I don't know much about how synapse works, so please forgive me if there are any mistakes here.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNo steps\n\n### Homeserver\n\n-\n\n### Synapse Version\n\nSynapse 1.82.0\n\n### Installation Method\n\npip (from PyPI)\n\n### Database\n\npgsql 15.2\n\n### Workers\n\nSingle process\n\n### Platform\n\nUbuntu 20.04\n\n### Configuration\n\n```yaml\r\ntrusted_key_servers: []\r\n```\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nThere is no relevant log.\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\nI looked up some similar issues beforehand, but no one seemed to have encountered such a large gap.",
